WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:07.840
Speaker 1: le to say that the dam is breaking&nbsp;
when it comes to Republicans and gun safety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:14.480
regulations. In fact, it's not breaking in&nbsp;
total. But we are starting to see some cracks as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:21.440
multiple Republicans, including an NRA endorsed&nbsp;
Republican, are now doing a 180 and saying it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.720
time for a gun safety regulation. Something has&nbsp;
to be done. I have two examples of that for you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.680
We're first going to look at an interview&nbsp;
that Republican Congressman Adam Kinzinger did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:38.640
on CNN. Now, caveats, Adam Kinzinger is leaving&nbsp;
Congress. Okay. Adam Kinzinger is not a Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.400
Republican. He is an anti-Trump Republican.&nbsp;
And so some people will write him off and say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.120
he's not really a Republican because of that.&nbsp;
But this is a Republican who for a long time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.560
opposed banning assault style rifles. And&nbsp;
now he said it's something he's open to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.760
This is a major change. Take a look at this.
Speaker 2: Congressman, you do still oppose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.320
a ban on the kind of assault weapons that&nbsp;
were used in the shooting. Can you explain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:09.920
why private citizens need weapons of war?
Speaker 3: Look, I have opposed a ban, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.760
fairly recently. I think I'm open to a ban&nbsp;
now. Well, it's going to depend on what it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.480
looks like because there's a lot&nbsp;
of nuances on what constitutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.560
you know, certain things. But I'm getting to&nbsp;
the point where I have to wonder, maybe it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.680
maybe somebody to own one. Maybe you need an extra&nbsp;
license, maybe you need extra training. And so the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.240
question is, is it a ban versus an additional&nbsp;
certification? But yeah, I got to tell you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.200
I mean, 99.9% of people that don't air, as we&nbsp;
all know, are not going to walk into a school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.520
and do this. But the problem is, for those&nbsp;
that support the Second Amendment, like me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.160
we have to be coming to the table with ways&nbsp;
to mitigate 18 year olds buying these guns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:51.120
and walking into schools. My side's not doing&nbsp;
that right. My side's not coming forward with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.360
reasonable ways to defend an amendment that we&nbsp;
think is very important there. And so I'm looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.760
at this going fine if people are going to put&nbsp;
forward solutions about certifying maybe who can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:05.040
buy an assault weapon. I'm certainly open to that.
Speaker 1: So listen, it's no big gun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:11.840
safety declaration. He's leaving Congress. He's&nbsp;
saying maybe it's just more restrictions and not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:19.440
really banning them, but it's a change and it's an&nbsp;
important change. Now, the reality is that a ban&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.400
alone isn't enough to really interrupt the&nbsp;
school shooting fiasco we have in this country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:30.560
But it's maybe one part and I talked about that&nbsp;
in my list of ten specific gun safety proposals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:36.640
that I outlined last week. It's also important to&nbsp;
mention Kinzinger still voted with Trump 90% of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:43.840
the time while Trump was president. So but listen,&nbsp;
he's willing here. Okay. And so let's let's praise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.640
it for what it is and not go overboard. Now,&nbsp;
here's another example then. Chris Jacobs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.880
who's a straight up NHRA, endorsed congressman&nbsp;
from New York after the Buffalo shooting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.600
He also says that his perspective has changed.&nbsp;
There's a great piece in The Buffalo News&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:06.320
which says Congressman Chris Jacobs of Orchard&nbsp;
Park made a surprising about face on gun control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:12.160
issues, becoming perhaps the first congressional&nbsp;
Republican to call for an assault weapons ban&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.120
in the wake of the recent mass shootings&nbsp;
in Buffalo and Duvall de Texas. At a news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.320
conference and later with the Buffalo News,&nbsp;
Jacobs, who was endorsed by the NRA in 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.480
laid out a series of new stances that run contrary&nbsp;
to the Republican Party line on guns. In addition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.800
to saying he would vote for a Democratic bill&nbsp;
banning assault weapons, he also said he would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:39.360
back raising the age on some gun purchases to&nbsp;
21. My suggestion was 25, but 2021 is something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:45.520
limiting the capacity of magazines. I agree. And&nbsp;
banning the sale of military style body armor to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.480
civilians. In the interview, Jacobs said the&nbsp;
two recent shootings forced him to reevaluate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.360
his position on guns and to research&nbsp;
where he wanted to stand in the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:04.080
So what can we say? I can't say the dam is&nbsp;
breaking. The NRA's incredibly strong, but there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:11.920
are cracks starting to form. And it really remains&nbsp;
to be seen whether this will become anything and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:18.880
whether anything will happen or not. This could&nbsp;
start to achieve change or at least start putting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:24.480
pressure on people to make a change. And it's&nbsp;
very interesting. Adam Kinzinger, Chris Jacobs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:30.400
let's see who else had themselves to the list.&nbsp;
The claim in Washington is that this is different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.560
Now we've heard that a thousand times&nbsp;
before because we've had a thousand or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:39.840
more mass shootings, but it remains to&nbsp;
be seen whether that will be the case

